-- Q3872: SOC Testing Controls [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under AT-C Section 320.41, roll-forward procedures extend interim testing conclusions to the end of the examination period by verifying that controls continued to operate effectively between the interim test date and period end. These may include inquiry, observation, re-performance, and additional transaction sampling.
Wrong (A): Procedures performed at the beginning of the period establish a baseline for interim testing but are not roll-forward procedures, which bridge the gap after interim testing.
Wrong (B): Roll-forward procedures extend testing within the current examination period, not to the next year. They bridge the gap between interim testing and period end.
Wrong (D): Roll-forward procedures require additional testing and evidence; they do not carry forward prior results without performing new procedures.$EXPL$
